  "question": {
    "text": "A body is projected at an angle of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>60</mn><mo>°</mo></math> with the horizontal. If its kinetic energy at its maximum height is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi></math>, then the height at which its potential energy and kinetic energy have equal values is&nbsp;(consider potential energy at the point of projection to be zero)",
